WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.100
Seen from Earth, two spaceships
fly straight at each other.

2
00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:06.920
One moves at six-tenths of light speed.

3
00:00:06.970 --> 00:00:09.580
The other moves at half light speed.

4
00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:12.580
Add those the everyday
way, as Galileo would,

5
00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:16.610
and each crew would see the other
coming at more than light speed.

6
00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:20.200
But Galileo's rules break
a postulate of relativity.

7
00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:23.960
So does either crew really
see the other beat light?

8
00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:27.170
In this mission, you'll meet
the Lorentz transformations,

9
00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:31.100
and see two observers disagree
about when things happen.

10
00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:33.420
Then you'll learn how
velocities really add,

11
00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:35.690
when they get close to light speed.

12
00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:39.440
Your mission: predict what each
crew measures for the other ship,

13
00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:40.990
and whether it beats light.
